# Spec §8.5. Telegram Desktop caches Mini App bundles somewhere its own
# cache-clear does not reach, and `index.html` is the one file in this build
# whose URL never changes — Vite content-hashes every asset it links to. A
# cached `index.html` therefore pins a client to a dead asset hash permanently,
# and the player sees a blank board with no way to fix it from their side.
#
# Both `/` and `/index.html` are listed because they are two URLs for one
# document and a rule on one does not cover the other. Everything else — the
# hashed `/assets/*.js` and `/assets/*.css` — is immutable by construction and
# deliberately left to the default long cache.
/
  Cache-Control: no-store, must-revalidate

/index.html
  Cache-Control: no-store, must-revalidate
